  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full-length concert at Cat's Cradle in Carrboro, North Carolina, on Saturday, December 18, 2021 [1][2]. This recording, captured and transferred by Liz Hamilton, is the only available audio for this specific date and consists of 24 songs spanning 118 minutes [1]. It is the 330th show in the archive's collection for the band, following a previous performance at the same venue on December 17, 2021 [2]. The setlist opens with a brief omicron reminder before launching into \"Michael Myers Resplendent\" from the album Heretic Pride [1]. The band then plays \"Lovecraft in Brooklyn,\" a track not heard in 59 archived shows, followed by \"Younger\" and \"In League with Dragons\" from the album In League with Dragons [1][2]. Other highlights include \"Pez Dorado\" and \"Tidal Wave\" from Getting Into Knives, and \"Maybe Sprout Wings\" from Get Lonely [1]. The performance features rare and bustout tracks such as \"From TG&Y,\" \"Isaiah 45:23,\" and \"Autoclave\" [1][2]. The set continues with songs from The Life of the World to Come, Beat the Champ, The Sunset Tree, and Tallahassee [1]. The main set concludes with \"Up the Wolves\" and \"You or Your Memory\" [1]. The encore includes five additional songs, ending with \"Spent Gladiator 2\" [1]. This recording offers a complete view of the band's live repertoire on that winter evening [1].",
